{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01HR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M \\mapsto \\widetilde M$", "MATH_0002": "$M \\mapsto M_{\\mathfrak p}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-abelian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39e0f2587f97cd55335ba6987f6f58b82e9fdecf8658750a23ac63359d408c43", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b785f36fdd474cc5f1259aed7ede0eae7a924d5af1005fd343124b887a85b136", "source_text": "Assertions (1) - (7) are clear from the discussion above.\nThe exactness of the functor <MATH_0001>\nfollows from the fact that the functor <MATH_0002>\nis exact and the fact that exactness of short exact sequences\nmay be checked on stalks, see\nModules, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9b9a533da0643890aff946f8f6c30de3717cd41a4479bebf3b40d696f4fb140d", "unit_id": "tag:01HV:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01HR", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-affine-scheme}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72f2b0124eafdd1da09167458b55c534aba1cfa49c955d32132784a32416dd19", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e29a3bda0ef7f6fdfd8f1d6e3dcf33eca970d1e9227a616c0dd09d829bacaf96", "source_text": "An <TEXTITOPEN_0001>affine scheme<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a locally ringed space isomorphic\nas a locally ringed space to <MATH_0001> for some ring <MATH_0002>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of affine schemes<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is a morphism in the category\nof locally ringed spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e2bdf17d96cc8a13fc9e6e7efb33871e60f0d6a25b6015f78d040eed988729fd", "unit_id": "tag:01HW:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01HR", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6850ee92a6fe384ee3f1326f36c4ffae8d362c1c10aca72201f53b9843da9f88", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that affine schemes play a special role\namong all locally ringed spaces, which is what the next\nsection is about.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3984723af9c1bdc3eba15f3a05a4c14fe10f0270898e133c04831203044e11d2", "unit_id": "tag:01HR:prose-0005"}
